6553	    /// Liveness (negative control) for the F6 fix above: proves the guard the
6554	    /// fizzle arm protects is real, so the positive test is not vacuous. If a
6555	    /// fizzled turn does NOT undo its tentative pop (the pre-fix behavior), the
6556	    /// next pass's step2 removal drain calls `remove_tid` while
6557	    /// `tentative_selection` is `Some`, and the run queue's transaction guard
6558	    /// panics. This is precisely the panic `undo_tentative_pop` prevents.
6559	    #[test]
6560	    #[should_panic(expected = "tentative_selection.is_none()")]
6561	    fn removal_drain_panics_if_tentative_window_left_open() {
